   $q$Which line marks the clearest shift in the speaker's understanding?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"The stakes stand behind us like a row of patient questions.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"imagery-not-shift"},{"text":"\"My aunt does not say anything about it.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character"},{"text":"\"It drips. It ticks. It shifts its weight like someone\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"imagery-not-shift"},{"text":"\"I used to think a record was a way of holding on.\"","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"I used to think a record was a way of holding on."$q$, $q$The words "I used to think" signal that the speaker's view is changing, and the next line states the new view. The lines about the "patient questions," the ticking ice, and the aunt's silence describe images or behavior rather than a change in the speaker's thinking.$q$, 'draft', '5014dedd-4788-5a9b-815f-3c11a732119c')
