   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Truly useful work comes from understanding what people actually need, not from impressive features.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Apps with more features are always more useful than simple ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Older people are unable to learn how to use new technology.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Volunteer ride programs help seniors reach the pharmacy and clinic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Truly useful work comes from understanding what people actually need, not from impressive features.$q$, $q$Marisol's feature-packed app goes unused, while the small tool built after watching the residents succeeds. The passage never says the residents cannot learn technology; it shows the clipboard already served them well.$q$, 'draft', 'f762e003-ca09-57c3-a8a2-d833a7afaabe')
