  ('5696b942-9491-5727-b030-90b4c3fd19ac', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the exchange "That's what you read. I asked what you know." develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals that Elan cheated by looking up moves during the game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Mr. Halvorsen thinks reading chess books is a waste of time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"It suggests that Mr. Halvorsen is angry about losing two games in a row.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It separates memorized information from real understanding, the difference Elan spends the summer learning.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It separates memorized information from real understanding, the difference Elan spends the summer learning.$q$, $q$Mr. Halvorsen contrasts reading with knowing, which names the gap in Elan's play. He calls it a "Good book," so he does not reject books, only reliance on them without understanding.$q$, 'draft', '9aea529c-f612-53d7-9bc0-132ec2e4b363')
