  ('221340b0-3a4b-5db4-9181-22d78458b658', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The root soli means "alone," and loqu means "speak." Why does Tobias's sister call his rehearsal a "soliloquy"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He was speaking aloud by himself with no real audience.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He was asking his sister to judge his performance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"He was arguing with an imaginary opposing team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He was reading his speech silently from his notes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He was speaking aloud by himself with no real audience.$q$, $q$A soliloquy is a speech made alone, and Tobias "rehearsed aloud" to a bookshelf. Reading silently ignores loqu, the root that means speaking.$q$, 'draft', 'a2ed043a-a576-5361-a12b-59833aa13adb')
