   $q$The root anthropo means "human," and morph means "form" or "shape." What makes the puppets "anthropomorphic"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They were made by humans rather than by machines.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"They are carved to look exactly like real animals.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"They can change shape when a child moves them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"They are animals given human clothing and features.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are animals given human clothing and features.$q$, $q$Anthropomorphic means given a human form, and the foxes and rabbits wear "waistcoats and bonnets" with "a painted human smile." Being handmade is true of many toys and does not capture the idea of an animal taking human form.$q$, 'draft', '2b8d33eb-bae9-53db-a112-7bad5ec265b4')
