   $q$The Greek root path can mean "disease," -logy means "study of," and -ist means "a person who." What do "pathologists" do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They design paths and trails through forests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"They study the way roots absorb water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They plant new trees after a forest is cut.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They study diseases and what causes them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They study diseases and what causes them.$q$, $q$Path (disease) plus -logy (study) plus -ist (person) gives "a person who studies disease," which matches scientists "identifying what makes plants sick." The English word path for a trail looks the same but is unrelated to the Greek root.$q$, 'draft', '995df5ae-8188-5b3e-9d61-2a6ea1f2e03c')
