  ('20a8e472-d1d7-5730-81d6-2c21072b2e2d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The prefix in- means "not," and the Latin root cred means "believe." What does it mean that Diego was "incredulous" about the tip?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He found the claim hard to believe.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He was angry that Elias had lied.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He did not understand the photo.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"He was excited to publish the claim.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He found the claim hard to believe.$q$, $q$Incredulous means "not believing," and Diego immediately asks how rare a real meteorite would be. He never says Elias lied, so anger at a lie goes beyond the text.$q$, 'draft', '059c876a-b458-587c-a6b4-bdc4eeabf8a8')
