  ('a1f22175-b736-5e24-a5ac-0e3c8ac54780', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The root cred means "believe," and the suffix -ence forms a noun naming a state or quality. What does Amara mean when she does not want to give the claim "any credence" yet?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She does not want to pay Elias for sending the photo.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"She does not want to print the photo because it is blurry.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"She does not want to criticize Elias in the newspaper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She does not want to accept it as true until it is checked.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She does not want to accept it as true until it is checked.$q$, $q$Credence is belief or acceptance, and Amara says the claim "needed checking" first. Paying someone relates to credit in the money sense, which is not what credence means here.$q$, 'draft', '059c876a-b458-587c-a6b4-bdc4eeabf8a8')
