  ('438c31b4-2b1d-56b2-aaa2-960e4ee23ac8', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The adjective "credible" means "believable," and the suffix -ity turns it into a noun. What would the paper lose if it lost "credibility" with readers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Readers' interest in science stories","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The right to print photographs of rocks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"The money it earns from advertisements","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"Readers' trust that its reporting is accurate","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Readers' trust that its reporting is accurate$q$, $q$Credibility is the quality of being believed, and Amara worries about printing something "wrong." Interest in science stories is related but narrower; the word is about whether readers believe the paper at all.$q$, 'draft', '059c876a-b458-587c-a6b4-bdc4eeabf8a8')
