   $q$The copyright paragraph depends most on which unstated assumption?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Paintings made after 1900 are never shown in the permanent galleries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-text"},{"text":"The gift shop earns more money than ticket sales do each year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-assumption"},{"text":"A private phone copy raises no legal issue that selling prints does not.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Visitors would rather buy postcards than take their own pictures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-reasoning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A private phone copy raises no legal issue that selling prints does not.$q$, $q$The author reasons that if the museum already prints and sells images, it "can hardly object" to private copies, which works only if a private copy creates no new legal problem. The passage says "nearly every" work is old, so it does not assume newer works are never shown.$q$, 'draft', '3ad6a6b9-6300-5439-8fed-2bc15355f38a')
