   $q$Which explanation does the historian argue is incomplete?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That the canal was built to carry grain and timber to Brissac.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-background-for-claim"},{"text":"That the railroad alone caused the canal to decline and close.","is_correct":true},{"text":"That drought made the upper locks too shallow for loaded boats.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-reasoning"},{"text":"That farmers preferred boats because rail rates were too high.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-claim-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That the railroad alone caused the canal to decline and close.$q$, $q$The historian says the familiar story is "tidy" but that the railroad only "delivered the final blow." The drought explanation is the historian's own view, not the one being challenged.$q$, 'draft', 'f4ad9a65-95ad-5369-877f-e13cfb2ac73c')
