   $q$Which additional evidence would most strengthen the author's use of other districts' results?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A list of the textbook titles that Fairhollow currently uses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-to-claim"},{"text":"A report on how many reading specialists Fairhollow employs now.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-to-claim"},{"text":"A survey showing that Linden Ridge students liked their tablets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-to-claim"},{"text":"Scores from a district that added tablets but made no other changes.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Scores from a district that added tablets but made no other changes.$q$, $q$A district that changed only to tablets would separate the effect of tablets from other changes, fixing the weakness in the Linden Ridge example. Student enjoyment does not show that tablets raised scores.$q$, 'draft', 'f703690a-a9cb-5303-a60e-c37844202b2b')
