  ('186110f3-8a54-5e2a-8882-5ac639825c43', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-argument-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The claim that plate size caused the drop in waste depends most on which assumption?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Menus and numbers of diners were similar in both kinds of weeks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students did not notice that the plates had changed size.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unnecessary-assumption"},{"text":"Eleven-inch plates are the standard size in most dining halls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-assumption"},{"text":"The newsletter reported the size of the drop correctly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-assumption"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Menus and numbers of diners were similar in both kinds of weeks.$q$, $q$If small-plate weeks happened to have different menus or fewer diners, those differences could explain less waste, and the passage does not rule this out. Students noticing the change would not undo the effect, since the argument is about how plate size limits servings.$q$, 'draft', '09d51f2c-d3a8-5f97-bdbb-771951c33afd')
