   $q$Which statement best expresses the author's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Error messages matter less than a polished visual design, which is what users notice and remember most.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"Error messages are the responsibility of support staff, who should be trained to explain the codes by phone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Error messages should be removed from software entirely because they only confuse and upset the people using it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"Error messages should be written clearly and respectfully because users depend on them when they are most frustrated.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Error messages should be written clearly and respectfully because users depend on them when they are most frustrated.$q$, $q$She asks developers to "write to our users, in their worst moment ... as though we respected them." She wants better messages, not none, and she says users study errors more than polished screens.$q$, 'draft', 'b47fab89-20d0-5a29-9d95-b3fde7b1f6f0')
