   $q$How does the author respond to the objection that friendly messages take too much time to write?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She agrees that deadlines make clear messages impossible and suggests that companies hire more writers instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"She ignores the objection and moves on to describe the visual design features that make software look polished.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"She admits she has cut that corner herself, then argues that the time saved is simply shifted onto users and support staff.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She dismisses the objection as an excuse and accuses developers of not caring about the people who use their programs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She admits she has cut that corner herself, then argues that the time saved is simply shifted onto users and support staff.$q$, $q$"I understand; I have shipped my share of mystery codes" concedes the point, and "The cost does not disappear. It moves" answers it. Her tone is sympathetic, not accusing, which keeps developers listening.$q$, 'draft', 'b47fab89-20d0-5a29-9d95-b3fde7b1f6f0')
