   $q$What role does the paragraph about safety play in the author's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It changes the subject from wildlife to staff schedules in order to show how hard the park employees work each year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It proves that no tree in the preserve will ever fall, so visitors no longer need to watch the path while walking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"It admits that the snags are dangerous, which weakens his argument but fulfills the park's legal duty to warn the public.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It answers an unspoken worry that could undercut his case, showing that leaving snags is a managed choice and not neglect.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It answers an unspoken worry that could undercut his case, showing that leaving snags is a managed choice and not neglect.$q$, $q$Readers convinced by the wildlife examples might still fear a falling tree, so he describes twice-yearly inspections and removal of leaning trees, ending with "The snags you see have been checked." He never claims no tree could ever fall.$q$, 'draft', 'cc97a657-c4a9-53ca-be12-656d8a1b34e2')
