-- Passage rg12-character-setting-plot-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2197d1eb-c5c8-5df6-85e4-fdbb2eed36e9', 'rg12-character-setting-plot-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Inventory$q$, $q$Forty spools of thread, sorted by a system
only my grandfather understood: not by color,
but by which customer had needed them last.
I lay them in a shoebox, and the shop gets quieter.

One tape measure, soft as a ribbon from use.
He wore it around his neck from the opening bell
until the lock turned at six, and when I was small
I thought it was part of him, like his glasses.

A chalk triangle worn down to a sliver.
With it he marked the hem of my first dress for a recital,
kneeling on this floor, telling me to stand straight
and stop looking at the mirror, because the mirror lies.

The landlord's letter sits on the cutting table
where the fabric used to be. It is polite. It is final.
The new tenant will sell phone cases, I am told,
and the window will be bright, and very clean.

I tape the last box shut and turn to go.
Then I take the chalk back out, the little sliver,
and on the inside of the door frame, low,
where no one cleaning will think to look,
I mark a hem line, straight, the way he taught me.$q$, 'draft')
