   $q$Why does the poet wait until the fourth stanza to mention the landlord's letter?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The letter is less important to the poem than the new tenant's plans for the window.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"Readers need the letter's legal details explained before they can understand the objects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"The letter arrives in the middle of the packing and surprises the speaker completely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Readers first know the shop as a place full of memory, so the news of its closing lands as a loss.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Readers first know the shop as a place full of memory, so the news of its closing lands as a loss.$q$, $q$Three stanzas of memories come before the "polite" and "final" letter, so the plot event carries emotional weight. The speaker is already packing, so the letter is not a surprise.$q$, 'draft', '2197d1eb-c5c8-5df6-85e4-fdbb2eed36e9')
