   $q$How does the opening description of the wash prepare for Ayse's discovery?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the canyon is full of plants, so finding a leaf is ordinary and expected.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It warns that the canyon walls are unstable, so the students must work quickly and carefully.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It presents a hot, lifeless place, so a fern from a wet swamp comes as a striking contrast.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains that the class came to the canyon specifically to search for fossil ferns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It presents a hot, lifeless place, so a fern from a wet swamp comes as a striking contrast.$q$, $q$"Nothing in the wash looked alive," and the floor held heat "like a stove," which makes the fern's swampy past surprising. The class was not told to look for ferns; Callum expected only mud.$q$, 'draft', '46712a2a-e724-56f6-ab07-0a50ff40c324')
