  ('bab208fa-a3f6-5554-9d92-0904f6711d07', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-character-setting-plot'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the author send Callum off to see the trackway before Ayse finds the leaf?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the trackway is the more important fossil and the real focus of the trip.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It explains why Ms. Halvorsen assigned the bottom band to Ayse in the first place.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It allows Callum to claim credit for the fern when he returns later in the afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It leaves Ayse alone to make the discovery, contrasting her patience with his chase after a known find.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It leaves Ayse alone to make the discovery, contrasting her patience with his chase after a known find.$q$, $q$Callum goes after prints "an earlier class had found," while Ayse, alone, uncovers something new. Callum never returns in the story, so he claims no credit.$q$, 'draft', '46712a2a-e724-56f6-ab07-0a50ff40c324')
