   $q$Which detail from Text 1 most closely matches the poem's line "I learned to run in colors not my own"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The light turns orange while Yusuf keeps clicking the counter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-match"},{"text":"Yusuf writes \"first year\" beneath the total on the form.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Mrs. Fairweather recalls the river running blue on Mondays and red by Thursday.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A silver flicker turns in the shallow pool below the ladder.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mrs. Fairweather recalls the river running blue on Mondays and red by Thursday.$q$, $q$Both describe the river colored by mill dye, which Mrs. Fairweather says changed "depending on what the dye vats were doing." The orange light is a color word, but it describes sunset, not the river's pollution.$q$, 'draft', 'f3773370-9e38-55ca-b9b8-ff228a411527')
