  ('cd9fa3f9-9e56-5516-9f82-1e1fa1bcbc93', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-connections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the 2003 specialist position connect to the coaches' original objection to rally scoring?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that coaches returned to side-out scoring for defensive players only.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows their fear about defense losing value was partly borne out, and the league moved to offset it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows their fear was mistaken, since defense became so important that a new position was needed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-relationship"},{"text":"It shows the league ignored their objection until television viewers asked for more defense.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows their fear about defense losing value was partly borne out, and the league moved to offset it.$q$, $q$Coaches feared rally scoring would hurt defensive teams (paragraph 3), and paragraph 5 says the specialist was added "partly to restore some of the value that defense had lost." Restoring lost value means the fear was partly realized, not mistaken.$q$, 'draft', '8639ec72-9f4f-5284-944c-db11d2789b21')
