  ('5710dba5-ac28-5e15-9f47-8116969e1e35', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-connections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$What larger point does the final paragraph make by tracing today's size charts back to the army records?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Modern size charts are still inaccurate because they rely on soldiers' measurements.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The army deserves more credit than tailors for the way Vellorians dress today.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Size charts should be revised more often because bodies and fashions change.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A tool built for one narrow, short-term purpose shaped a lasting system far beyond it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A tool built for one narrow, short-term purpose shaped a lasting system far beyond it.$q$, $q$The closing sentence stresses that the records "were never meant to clothe anyone but soldiers," yet every later chart descends from them. The passage notes regular revisions, so it does not claim today's charts are still based only on soldiers.$q$, 'draft', '808ede3a-4c5b-588c-9124-0ef5b93698a5')
