   $q$In paragraph 4, tardigrades appear "impervious" to harm. Which meaning fits this context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"permanently changed by it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"easily injured by it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"unaware that it exists","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"not affected or damaged by it","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$not affected or damaged by it$q$, $q$Tuns exposed to cold, radiation, and pressure "revived afterward with no apparent damage," so impervious means not affected by harm. "Permanently changed" contradicts the phrase "no apparent damage."$q$, 'draft', '9e2ee895-e308-57c5-b15f-9300a0d96898')
