   $q$Which meaning of "redundant" fits the way engineers use it in paragraph 3?$q$, $q$[{"text":"sent from the spacecraft several times each day","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"shortened so that it can be sent more quickly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"useless because it only repeats something already said","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"containing deliberate extra information that repeats the original","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$containing deliberate extra information that repeats the original$q$, $q$The author contrasts the engineering sense with everyday speech: in engineering, redundancy is "deliberate and valuable," made of "extra bits that repeat information." The "useless" meaning is the everyday sense the author explicitly sets aside with "though."$q$, 'draft', 'b5daaae5-9194-5836-95e3-35c06ad73cef')
