  ('cabaaf2f-9338-5687-acf7-157a1755e390', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which conclusion about the system's effects on Lake Orrin is best supported by the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"No harm has been detected yet, but the evidence cannot rule out slow changes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The warm plume has already reduced the number of fish near the outflow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The system has been proven harmless, so further monitoring is a formality.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"The lake's warm and cold layers have begun to mix because of the outflow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$No harm has been detected yet, but the evidence cannot rule out slow changes.$q$, $q$Ashdown has found no change in fish numbers but warns that three years may be too short for "slow effects" to appear. Calling the system proven harmless ignores that warning and the decade of further study the university is funding.$q$, 'draft', '5d129fe6-6231-5d60-be2c-59bb5eb7dcc5')
