   $q$According to the passage, what does a "best before" date mainly indicate?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The point after which the food's quality may decline.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The last day on which the food is safe to eat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"The date on which the food was packed and sealed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The day by which a store must remove the food from sale.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The point after which the food's quality may decline.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says a "best before" date "is about quality" and the food is usually still safe afterward. Safety is the meaning of a "use by" date, which is the confusion the passage describes.$q$, 'draft', '62364ea3-50e5-5cde-823f-94a681738d37')
