  ('d8ac30d0-cdad-5019-890e-19529b584bf3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-evidence-inference'), null, 'easy',
   $q$According to the passage, why do trees in the same region share a similar pattern of rings?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are usually cut down in the same season by the same builders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They belong to the same species, and each species grows at one rate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They all experience the same weather, which sets the width of each ring.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They grow in the same soil, which adds exactly one ring every year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They all experience the same weather, which sets the width of each ring.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says "all the trees in a region experience the same weather," and weather determines whether a ring is wide or narrow. The passage says trees add one ring a year but never credits soil for the shared pattern.$q$, 'draft', '84a87d3c-09bb-5f91-859b-369e6b10e2d8')
