   $q$Why could Iqbal date the felling of only nine of the fourteen beams precisely?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The other five had been damaged when the cores were drilled from the beams.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Only those nine were made of oak, the species covered by the reference sequence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The other five were too old to match any part of the reference sequence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Only those nine kept the outermost ring that records the tree's last year of growth.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Only those nine kept the outermost ring that records the tree's last year of growth.$q$, $q$The nine beams still had their ring "just beneath the bark," while the others had outer rings "trimmed away when the beams were squared." All fourteen are described as oak beams, so species is not the difference.$q$, 'draft', '84a87d3c-09bb-5f91-859b-369e6b10e2d8')
