   $q$Which evidence best supports Iqbal's conclusion that the barn was most likely raised in 1743 or shortly after?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Local tradition held that the barn dated from some time in the 1600s.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"},{"text":"Two of the beams contain no growth ring later than the year 1528.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"The reference sequence for local oaks reaches back over eight hundred years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Nine beams were felled in 1742 or 1743, and builders then used timber soon after cutting.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Nine beams were felled in 1742 or 1743, and builders then used timber soon after cutting.$q$, $q$The felling dates combined with the practice of working timber "soon after felling" lead directly to 1743. The beams with rings ending in 1528 support the idea of reuse, not the building date.$q$, 'draft', '84a87d3c-09bb-5f91-859b-369e6b10e2d8')
